{
  "name": "openrouter-endpoints",
  "kind": "endpoints",
  "source": "OpenRouter's public endpoint list per model, GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models/<author>/<slug>/endpoints (no key), each endpoint's provider_name, tag, quantization, whether supported_parameters holds seed, and pricing.prompt, pricing.completion and pricing.input_cache_read in dollars per token, multiplied here by one million",
  "fetched": "2026-11-26",
  "unit": "US dollars per million tokens",
  "rule": "Pre-registration, Models: each model and both judges pinned to the maker's own endpoint where OpenRouter lists one, otherwise the cheapest endpoint that honours seed, with allow_fallbacks false. A pin is openrouter_provider {order: [tag], allow_fallbacks: false}.",
  "notes": [
    "Each response was read once on the day fetched, saved, and hashed as served (response_sha256); the endpoint list is volatile, and an endpoint gone on the day of a run fails that run's first call under allow_fallbacks false, which is the registered behaviour: the list is read again and the new pin is its own PR, before the run starts.",
    "deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro-0813: the maker's own endpoint (DeepSeek, tag deepseek) does not list seed among its supported parameters; the rule names the maker's endpoint first, so M1 is pinned to it and the seed the runner sends is not honoured upstream (decision 2026-11-26-r6-decision-m1-maker-endpoint-without-seed).",
    "openai/gpt-5.4: OpenAI lists three endpoints of its own (openai, openai/flex, openai/fast); B1 is pinned to the standard tier, tag openai (decision 2026-11-26-r6-decision-b1-standard-tier).",
    "Prices are each endpoint's list price on the day fetched, not what the ledger meters (pi-ai's catalogue price, model.cost) and not a quote."
  ],
